<title>POLAND: Espebepe plunges on bankruptcy threat.</title>
<headline>Espebepe plunges on bankruptcy threat.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish construction company Espebepe SA extended its 45.2-percent fall since October 22 when it said it could go bankrupt, falling 10 percent to 3.15 zlotys in a 0.8-million-zloty turnover, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's hard to say what will happen with the stock, but at least selling was not that strong after price fixing as it was during the last sessions,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>The company said last week it could go bankrupt if its creditors did not agree for a debt-write-off deal.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
